# Auto-deploy to main

After finishing a batch of site/marketing edits in this repo, **commit and push to `origin/main` without waiting to be asked**, so Vercel can deploy to runbloom.ai.

## When

- Applies to completed work that should go live (HTML, copy, assets, deck, timeline, LinkedIn drafts, brand docs used by the site).
- Skip only if the user explicitly says not to push, or if changes are clearly WIP / exploratory and they asked to hold.

## How

1. Follow the normal git safety protocol (status, diff, log; HEREDOC commit message; no force; no amend unless rules allow).
2. Stage relevant files only (no secrets).
3. Commit with a concise why-focused message.
4. `git push -u origin HEAD` (or `git push` when tracking exists).
5. Tell the user the commit SHA and that it is on `main` / deploying.

Do not ask “want me to commit and push?” for routine site updates in this repo.
